{"title":"Career Roadmap · Sales Executive","role":"Sales Executive","summary":"A Sales Executive is responsible for generating business by identifying prospects, understanding customer needs, presenting products or services, handling objections, negotiating, closing deals, and maintaining customer relationships.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"B.Com – Marketing / Retail / HR provides a reasonable foundation for this career. Marketing and Retail are the strongest direct alignments, while HR can support sales through communication, relationship management, negotiation, and people skills."},{"type":"p","text":"For long-term growth, the student should progress beyond basic selling into B2B sales, key-account management, business development, sales analytics, CRM, sales operations, or sales leadership."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","Typical Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Sales Foundation"},{"text":"B.Com + communication + selling + CRM + internships"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Sales & Business Development"},{"text":"Sales Executive, Business Development Executive, Account Executive"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Sales Management"},{"text":"Senior Sales Executive, Key Account Manager, Area Sales Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Commercial Leadership"},{"text":"Regional Sales Manager, National Sales Manager, Sales Head"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the B.Com Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Business & Communication Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build knowledge in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Principles of marketing"},{"text":"Business communication"},{"text":"Business economics"},{"text":"Accounting"},{"text":"Business management"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Organizational behaviour"},{"text":"Business mathematics"},{"text":"Introduction to retail"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Professional speaking"},{"text":"Presentation skills"},{"text":"Business writing"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Questioning techniques"},{"text":"Negotiation fundamentals"},{"text":"Telephone etiquette"},{"text":"Email communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A sales professional must be able to understand the customer before attempting to sell."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Sales & Marketing Core"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical understanding of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Sales"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prospecting"},{"text":"Lead generation"},{"text":"Lead qualification"},{"text":"Customer needs analysis"},{"text":"Product presentation"},{"text":"Objection handling"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Closing techniques"},{"text":"Follow-up"},{"text":"Relationship management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Marketing"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Market segmentation"},{"text":"Targeting"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Marketing mix"},{"text":"Digital marketing"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Brand management"},{"text":"Competitor analysis"},{"text":"Customer journey"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Retail"},{"type":"p","text":"For students choosing the Retail pathway:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Store operations"},{"text":"Merchandising"},{"text":"Inventory management"},{"text":"Retail pricing"},{"text":"Customer experience"},{"text":"Visual merchandising"},{"text":"Point-of-sale systems"},{"text":"Retail analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Sales Readiness"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus on actual selling capability."},{"type":"h","text":"CRM"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn platforms such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Salesforce"},{"text":"HubSpot"},{"text":"Zoho CRM"},{"text":"Microsoft Dynamics"}]},{"type":"p","tex